  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n   We need to minimize the maximum overlap integral C5. \n   Previous approaches used local optimization but might get stuck in traps.\n   This new approach uses a multi-resolution strategy with aggressive dimensionality reduction: \n   - Start from low dimensions and gradually move to higher dimensions\n   - In each dimension, we use differential evolution (genetic-like search) then polish with bounded optimization\n   - Solutions are evaluated on the original high dimension to prevent local optima\n   - Time is tracked and budgets allocated to balance exploration and exploitation\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n   Let n_base = 2^start_level to 2^max_level with steps.\n   Objective: maximize min_{steps} which targets the worst overlap\n   Transformation: map low-dimensional solutions to high-dimensional spaces via interpolation\n   Progressively integrate results from lower to higher dimensions\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n   Parameters:\n     - start_level=3, max_level=9 (powers of 2 up to 512)\n     - trials_per_level=12 (independent evaluations)\n     - stage_powers=[2,3,4,5] (progressive evaluation for escaping local optima)\n\n   For thislevel from start_level to max_level:\n     1. Create candidates in dimension n_low = 2^thislevel\n     2. Differential evolution:\n        - Population size=100, max_iter=50\n        - Bracketing with six bounces to escape\n        - Projection based on interior point barrier smoothing\n     3. Identify best candidate from this level\n     4. Carefully map to high dimension using interpolation\n     5. Final high-dimension validation and polish with trust-region reflector\n     6. Track improvements using Kadane's algorithm\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n   We'll implement:\n   - Coarse-to-fine integration through dimension stepping\n   - Population transformation between dimensions\n   - Quality control with adaptive confidence thresholds\n   - Budget scheduling to preserve explorative behavior\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n   Processing stages:\n   - 50 seconds for initial local optimal finding\n   - 30 seconds for low-frequency dimension stepping\n   - Remaining for final high-dimension optimization\n   Implement early termination checks\n   Use exponential backoff for failed constraints\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n   Must validate:\n   - Sum strictly equals expected value\n   - Strict 0\u2264function\u22641 enforcement\n   - Max correlation identically computes\n   Export as (best_h, best_c5, n_high) with clear metadata below\n   Use numpy.testing.assert_approx_equal strictly",
